This project has the option to link to and uses CamillaDSP, which is available under 
the Mozilla Public License 2.0 (MPL-2.0).
The source code for CamillaDSP can be found at: https://github.com/HEnquist/camilladsp

The pure Swift DSP engine included in this project is a clean-room port of the
CamillaDSP concepts and configuration format. It is a completely different underlying
implementation, built from scratch in Swift, and is not subject to or released
under CamillaDSP's original MPL-2.0 license. 

In most cases, the Swift engine's zero-allocation, SIMD-optimized implementation
is significantly more computationally efficient than its Rust counterpart, and it
supports additional features (such as Apple's native CoreAudio resampler and DSD
over PCM (DoP) support) not present in the original Rust engine.
